================================================================================
WHY THIS LINE EXISTS
================================================================================

bERP HRMS's `main` branch tracks upstream's develop lane and is 17.0.0-dev. It
declares frappe >=17.0.0-dev,<18.0.0, and bench compares that with
semantic_version, so it cannot be installed on a released v16 bench at all.

Everything bERP runs outside CI is released v16:

    bERP development VM        frappe 16.33.1, erpnext 16.34.2, no HR app
    Tenants                    released v16, HR from upstream hrms@version-16

This line declares frappe >=16.0.0,<17.0.0 and erpnext >=16.0.0,<17.0.0, which
both of those satisfy. It is what makes bERP's own HR fork installable on a
bench that exists.

It does not replace the tenant app on its own. Tenant HR is upstream
hrms@version-16 until bstBizEra/bERP's scripts/apps/pins.json says otherwise,
and moving an existing site is a migration rather than an install --
docs/RENAME_TO_BERP_HRMS.md has the runbook. docs/VERSION-16.md explains how
this line, `main`, and upstream `hrms` relate.

`main` and this branch share no bERP history. Each was cut from its own upstream
lane, so a change wanted on both is applied to both rather than merged between
them.

NOT THE SAME AS THIS REPOSITORY'S `version-16` BRANCH. That branch was cut from
the same upstream commit and does something deliberately smaller: it changes two
title strings and leaves app_name as `hrms`, so it drops into a tenant's
existing `hrms` app slot with no migration at all. It is live, and a tenant
branding cutover pins it at 4be6d4e8bf0b964cb8f5d00ecf68f40889e779a0. This
branch renames the app instead, which is what makes it a separate app slot and
what makes installing it onto a site that already has `hrms` a migration. Both
are wanted; they are not alternatives to each other.

