================================================================================
MODIFICATIONS FROM UPSTREAM
================================================================================

  Renamed -- the application installs as `berp_hrms`, not as `hrms`:

      The Python package moved from hrms/ to berp_hrms/, and every lowercase
      `hrms` token in the application tree became `berp_hrms`: imports and
      dotted paths, patch paths, /assets/ URLs, desk bundle names, realtime and
      cache keys, the PWA route, and the "app" field on Dock, Desktop Icon,
      Workspace and Sidebar fixtures. Four spellings were deliberately kept --
      github.com/frappe/hrms, the [org_name]/hrms example in config/docs.py, the
      sk_hrms site-config key, and upstream's [frappe.hrms] Crowdin project id.
      Outside the application tree the root hrms.png, the .github/hrms-*.png
      screenshots and .github/helper/documentation.py were left as committed.

      app_title became "bERP HR" and app_publisher became bstBizEra. Product
      copy inside the application still reads "Frappe HR" and is unchanged.

      No application logic was modified. Every change is a substitution of the
      package name, and `git log` on any file still shows its upstream
      authorship. The repository's own formatters were then re-run at the
      versions .pre-commit-config.yaml pins, because the longer package name
      pushes some import blocks and call expressions past the configured widths.

      The consequence is that `git merge upstream/version-16` now conflicts
      across the tree; docs/RENAME_TO_BERP_HRMS.md records the exact
      substitution rule so a sync reproduces it rather than inventing one.

      Two comment-only exceptions: hooks.py and api/oauth.py each carry a
      `# nosemgrep` annotation, because rewriting the package name inside the
      flagged code made two already-triaged inherited findings read as new ones
      to semgrep. docs/SECURITY-BASELINE.md records the exception, and measures
      that the rename introduced no new finding: 87 on the unmodified upstream
      tree, 85 here, the difference being exactly those two. No executable line
      changed.

  Added:
      berp_hrms/rename_migration.py   In-place hrms -> berp_hrms migration for a
                                      site that already has hrms installed
      berp_hrms/commands.py           Registers `bench rename-from-hrms`, the
                                      only way to reach that migration: bench
                                      execute refuses a dotted path in an app
                                      the site has not installed yet
      docs/VERSION-16.md              What this line is for, and how to install
                                      it on a v16 bench
      docs/RENAME_TO_BERP_HRMS.md     The substitution rule and the site runbook
      docs/SECURITY-BASELINE.md       Inherited-findings policy and inventory
      .github/workflows/README.md     Which inherited workflows were removed
      NOTICE

  Removed -- seven workflows that operated upstream's project rather than this
  one, three of which held contents: write:
      build-and-commit-assets.yml     on_release.yml
      build_image.yml                 release_notes.yml
      generate-pot-file.yml           stale.yml
      initiate_release.yml

  Modified:
      .github/workflows/patch.yml     The v14 dump CI restores is a site with
                                      UPSTREAM `hrms` installed. The historical
                                      legs now run against upstream hrms, and
                                      the swap to this repository happens
                                      through `bench rename-from-hrms` -- the
                                      path a real site takes.
      .github/workflows/labeller.yml  Granted pull-requests: write. The default
                                      token is read-only, so the action failed
                                      the first time a pull request matched a
                                      rule in .github/labeler.yml.

  Deliberately NOT carried over from `main`: scripts/deploy-dev.sh,
  scripts/deploy-production.sh, scripts/setup-bench.sh,
  scripts/install-berp-apps.sh, docs/LOCAL_SETUP.md, docs/DEPLOYMENT.md,
